Z||000000||Monkeyman||07-03-2001||07:25 PM||||If you're reading this, you're still around.  Let me just take this opportunity to say a few things.  If and when Cliff decides to reopen the forum to the public, I hope that some of the lower forms of life are gone.  I can't believe how things have gotten around here.  Just a few bad apples really *did* spoil the bunch.  I won't name names, but those who have spoiled things know who they are.  Maybe time will mature them.  Thank God Cliff has a back door.  I honestly don't know what I'd do without this forum.  I've acquired 2 of my 4 Fieros through the forum and fixed many things, found many parts, etc, etc because of PFF.  I've met a ton of great folks, too.  I'm sooooo glad that Cliff allowed me to stay.  I hope he feels better soon and feels like reopening the forum.  If not, at least I'll have some very valuable resources at hand.<P>I'm rambling.  Just glad that I still have a Fiero home to go to.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">  <P>Cliff--If you decide to reopen the forum and wish to delete this thread, feel free although I will happily stand behind my words.<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||07-03-2001||07:30 PM||||Hey Dave,<P>It's not really a backdoor. In fact, everybody can still access this place although no longer through the main page anymore. Everybody who has one of the forum's pages in their browser's cache can get here.<P>So in all probability, most people can still get here...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mach10||07-03-2001||07:31 PM||||I found my way in too.<BR>I cannot say how saddened I am. I hate this, but I WILL accept Cliff's final decision.<BR>I've had nothing but good times here, odly enough, only to be spoilt by some dicksmack as$hole today. Go figure. <P>Cliff: I hope you reconsider. Truly. If not, I respect your descision. If you do, why not spread the load a little. You are right, the forum has grown large. Pick some more stable members, and give them the hammer of justice. A small garden's easy to manage, but when it gets big, you need to start weeding. I say less topic moderation, and more banning, temporary or otherwise. If you come back, toughen things up. 95% of the forum won't even have to deal with this.<P>I am SO mad right now...||||reg||9
Z||000003||Slammed Fiero||07-03-2001||07:45 PM||||How about make a subscription fee. (yearly)<P>That weeds out a lot of people who<P>#1 post for the reason of selling then leaving<BR>#2 conforms the list a little more , you pay to get on , you have no "right" to say what ever you want because you pay to be here. This also helps to combat multiple user names, and Fraud in selling parts online , since you could request some personal information when a person has a request for subscription.<P>I think this can be seen as an oppertunity for cliff to recoop some funds lost.<P>Open up a US account. Use Paypal to take subscription orders.<P>This place is too valuable and I think we all took it for granted.<P>Jonathan M. MCCreery||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||07-03-2001||07:55 PM||||The people that are up in arms need to stop responding to the posts (just like I am??!). There will always be people flaming, people mis-understanding, people calling a spade a spade and on and on. There's no way it can be stopped but we can certainly stop encouraging the behavour by IGNORING it.<P>What goes on outside the forum can't be controlled. What goes on inside can. <P>I will be lucky to meet 1 out of the 1000+ people that have floated through here. What people say in the end is irrelevant to my life and those that feel flamed should come to grips with the same.<P>And now back to the Rubbermaid cup holder thread already in progress.......<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 07-03-2001).]||||reg||1
