Z||000008||hugh||07-04-2001||08:49 AM||||Ever since I read Cliff's announcement I've been thinking there should be a charge for the use of this forum.If there were a yearly charge,it could make a difference.Why should Cliff pay and work to make it better for us?I for one have no trouble with paying a fee to post a response,start a thread,or ask a question.If we paid $24 a year,that's only $2 a month,and for the majority that is less than ONE CENT a minute to enjoy one of our favorite things.For those that smoke,that is probably less than you spend a day($2) to buy smokes.I spend too much time here(to the detriment of other things),but I would miss the camaraderie and the people I have come to regard as friends.<BR>           Bottom line;I will do whatever is required of me to keep this forum operating!!!  ||||reg||1
Z||000009||mbramble||07-04-2001||09:26 AM||||Personally, I don't think it's a money problem.  If it were then Cliff would have started charging a long time ago.  There have been many offers to pay a 'subscription' or provide donations to Cliff on these pages before but he has never accepted them.  This is something that Cliff has taken on to support the Fiero community.  Having said that, if it is because of money, I would gladly pay.<P>I think it has more to do with the lack of respect and regard for others that has him upset.  Not to mention the personal verbal assaults on him.  There is just too much garbage that is spewed that has nothing to do with Fieros and is not of broad common interest to the Forum at large.<P>Then, when you start paying, how long will it be before the first post gets deleted/closed and the originator comes back complaining that he is a paying customer and has a right to say whatever he wants.  I'm sure that would not be the case as Cliff is savvy enough to have us sign a "acceptable standards of conduct" that would "allow" him to delete anything he desired even if we were paying.  <P>I'd just as soon see the O/T section go away and focus on discussions, troubleshooting, and modifications to our Fieros.  The unbridled lack of respect for others that gets started in the O/T section quickly spills over into the meat of this Forum -- the Technical and General Fiero sections (and the buying/selling of Fiero items in the Mall).  Instead of answering a question or providing input, the responses quickly become little inside jokes that were started in O/T.<P>It would be a savings of time and resources to Cliff if all these ridiculous signatures would go away and a group of people didn't feel that they must respond to every thread just to up their post count or whatever reason causes them to make a post that says essentially "I don't have an answer to your question but here I am anyway".  Cutting out that and the endless, mindless posts about one forum memebr or another would probably reduce the resources required to operate this site by half.  Without losing anything of value to people who need information about their Fieros.  (If you just have a desire to show your Fiero to others, put photos of it up on a photo site and post a link to that as you sig - that makes your pride and joy available for others to see and is a negligible drain of the Forums resources.)<P>My 2 cents....<p>[This message has been edited by mbramble (edited 07-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||Philphine||07-04-2001||10:06 AM||||a small problem with paying is then someone just as bothersome but still willing to pay would really feel they have a right to say and do what they want. i wouldn't mind a small subscription fee. i pay for magazines but still use this more.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>SERENITY NOW!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000011||Monkeyman||07-04-2001||01:48 PM||||My point regarding a subscription fee is this...It's probable that some of the troublemakers won't be willing to pay money just so they can cause trouble.  Only the more serious Fieroholics would be willing to pay, IMO.  Why would somebody spend their hard earned money just to post a few worthless remarks, especially when they know that they could be booted out (according to an "acceptable standards of conduct" agreement) and lose their money.  Of course, all of this is pointless since Cliff has already made it clear that he refuses to take any money for his work.  Once again, 'You da man, Cliff'.<P>Just my two cents worth. <P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM<p>[This message has been edited by Monkeyman (edited 07-04-2001).]||||reg||1
